(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff strain gauge / resistor bridge input channel process image.
</summary>
<description>
Represents EL3356/EL3356-0010 input PDO 0x1A00 with 16-bit Status and PDO 0x1A01 with signed 32-bit Value.
Both input PDOs are required. Link Status to RMB Status and Value to RMB Value (INT32) separately;
PDO 0x1A01 alone does not contain status information.
Select the integer assignment; REAL load and two-channel voltage modes require different types.
Calibration and device settings determine engineering scaling. Evaluate Status before using Value.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE STRAIN_GAUGE_INPUT_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	Status AT %I* : WORD;
	Value AT %I* : DINT;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
